---
import AroundScreen from "./AroundScreen.astro";
import SourceBadge from "./SourceBadge.astro";
import { sidebars } from "./data";

interface Props { home: string; world: string; }
const { home, world } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="world-lab-screen" id="relay">
        <header class="world-lab-screen-head"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Screen 08 · Hara Relay</p><h2>Automate selection and drafting; keep publication accountable.</h2></div><p>Relay watches top stories, repositories, clips, and releases, then generates channel-specific drafts behind rate limits and human approval.</p></header>
        <div class="world-lab-canvas around-lab-canvas">
          <AroundScreen current="relay" mainId="around-relay-content" sidebarTitle="Hara Relay" sidebarGroups={sidebars.relay} sidebarNote="Prototype only: this visual-language screen performs no network actions and publishes nothing." home={home} world={world}>
            <Fragment slot="actions"><a class="hara-v2-button" href="#radar">Open radar</a><a class="hara-v2-button">Edit policy</a><a class="hara-v2-button" data-variant="primary">Approve selected ↗</a></Fragment>
            <div class="around-heading"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Outbound automation</p><h1>Top signals become accountable drafts.</h1><p>Selection is rule-driven. Publication remains channel-specific, attributable, rate-limited, and reviewable.</p></div><span class="hara-v2-badge" data-tone="success">Policy active</span></div>
            <section class="around-relay-grid"><div class="around-panel around-queue"><header><h2>Candidate queue</h2><button>Re-score</button></header><article class="is-selected"><SourceBadge source="world" label="Story" /><p><b>LiveSession discussion</b><span>Score 92 · canonical record linked</span></p></article><article><SourceBadge source="github" /><p><b>std.typed release</b><span>Score 87 · release velocity</span></p></article><article><SourceBadge source="world" label="Clip" /><p><b>Snippet of the day</b><span>Score 81 · curator pick</span></p></article></div><div class="around-panel around-draft"><header class="around-section-head"><div><p class="hara-v2-kicker">Generated draft</p><h2>LiveSession discussion</h2></div><SourceBadge source="x" label="Outbound X" /></header><div class="around-toolbar"><div><button aria-pressed="true">X</button><button>Reddit</button><button>Weekly digest</button><button>World</button></div></div><div class="around-post"><div class="around-author"><span>H</span><p><b>@hara_lang</b><small>Hara Relay · automated draft</small></p></div><p>One lifecycle now governs Hara’s interpreted and compiled browser sessions: stale-command fencing, ordered events, explicit capabilities, and transactional restart.</p><div class="around-link-card"><b>Browser sessions without browser-only semantics</b><small>Canonical implementation plus attributed discussion</small></div><footer><span>238 / 280</span><span>Sources included</span></footer></div><label class="around-field"><span>Approval note</span><textarea>Lead with the canonical merge. Use external discussion as context, not authority.</textarea></label><footer><button class="hara-v2-button">Reject</button><button class="hara-v2-button">Regenerate</button><button class="hara-v2-button" data-variant="primary">Approve for 18:30</button></footer></div></section>
            <section class="around-policy"><div><i></i><p><b>Human approval required</b><span>External-author content never auto-publishes.</span></p></div><div><i></i><p><b>Maximum two posts daily</b><span>Channel-specific rate limit.</span></p></div><div><i></i><p><b>Canonical link first</b><span>Repository or Hara story leads.</span></p></div><div><i></i><p><b>Attribution locked</b><span>Original platforms remain visible.</span></p></div></section>
            <Fragment slot="aside">
              <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Selection policy</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body around-kv"><div><span>Minimum score</span><b>80</b></div><div><span>Source percentile</span><b>top 10%</b></div><div><span>Canonical record</span><b>required</b></div><div><span>Human approval</span><b>required</b></div></div></section>
              <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Today · Melbourne</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body around-schedule"><div><time>09:00</time><p><b>GitHub release</b><span>Published · X</span></p></div><div><time>13:00</time><p><b>Snippet of the day</b><span>Published · World</span></p></div><div><time>18:30</time><p><b>LiveSession story</b><span>Awaiting approval</span></p></div></div></section>
              <section class="hara-v2-panel"><header class="hara-v2-panel-header"><h2>Publication receipt</h2></header><div class="hara-v2-panel-body"><p class="world-aside-copy">A successful effect records score, sources, generated draft, edits, approver, policy version, and channel response.</p></div></section>
            </Fragment>
          </AroundScreen>
        </div>
        <div class="world-lab-notes"><article><b>Automate reversible work</b><p>Discovery, scoring, clustering, and drafts can run continuously.</p></article><article><b>Channel-specific drafts</b><p>Each destination receives an appropriate structure.</p></article><article><b>Receipts over vibes</b><p>Every outbound effect records why, who, policy, and result.</p></article></div>
      </section>
